## Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `BEDROCK_MODEL` | Default model when none is selected — same role as `COPILOT_MODEL`/`MOONSHOT_MODEL` on other providers; catalog aliases work (`claude-opus-4-8`) | `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| `BEDROCK_PROVIDER` | Manual schema override: `anthropic` / `claude`, `openai` / `gpt`, `converse` / `auto` | auto-detect |
| `BEDROCK_TEMPERATURE` | Temperature (used by OpenAI and Converse paths) | — |
| `BEDROCK_TOP_P` | Top-p sampling (used by the Converse path) | — |
| `BEDROCK_REGION` | AWS region (takes precedence over `AWS_REGION`) | — |
| `AWS_REGION` | AWS region (fallback) | — |
| `AWS_PROFILE` | Profile in `~/.aws/credentials` or `~/.aws/config` (SSO, assume-role). Can be set in `.env`. | — |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | Static credentials | — |
| `AWS_CA_BUNDLE` | PEM bundle read natively by SDK v2 | — |
| `BEDROCK_BASE_URL` | Custom base URL for the whole Bedrock surface — runtime and model listing (VPC endpoints, corporate DNS) — parity with Claude Code's `ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_BASE_URL`; wins over `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL*` | — |
| `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK_RUNTIME` | Override for Bedrock Runtime endpoint | — |
| `BEDROCK_CONTROL_BASE_URL` | Optional control-plane override (model listing) when it lives on a different host than `BEDROCK_BASE_URL` — VPC endpoints are per service; wins over `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK` | inherits `BEDROCK_BASE_URL` |
| `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK` | Override for Bedrock (control plane) endpoint | — |
| `AWS_EC2_METADATA_DISABLED` | `true` explicitly disables IMDS (169.254.169.254) | — |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_ENABLE_IMDS` | `1`/`true` forces IMDS probe on non-EC2 machines | `false` |
| `BEDROCK_MAX_TOKENS` | Output token limit | From catalog |
| `BEDROCK_ANTHROPIC_ENDPOINT` | Claude wire routing: `auto` (default — catalog decides, with Mantle→InvokeModel fallback on failure), `mantle` (pins the Messages endpoint, no fallback) or `invoke` (legacy InvokeModel only) | `auto` |
| `BEDROCK_MANTLE_BASE_URL` | Messages endpoint override (`bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws`) for VPC endpoints/proxies | — |
| `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` | Short-lived bearer token (`aws-bedrock-token-generator`) — sent in the Messages endpoint's `x-api-key` header, no SigV4 | — |
| `ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS` | Alternative shared with direct Anthropic provider | — |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_CA_BUNDLE` | Bedrock-specific PEM bundle (overrides `AWS_CA_BUNDLE`) | — |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY` | `true` disables TLS verification (insecure) | `false` |
| `HTTPS_PROXY` / `HTTP_PROXY` / `NO_PROXY` | Standard Go/SDK HTTP proxy | — |

**Default model:** `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`
**Default region:** `us-east-1`

All these vars surface in `/config providers` (chat) and `/config quality` (embeddings). See [Environment Variables](/reference/environment-variables) for the full reference.

