===== FILE: reference/api/acknowledge-incident.mdx =====
TITLE: Acknowledge Incident

# Acknowledge Incident

  Name of the Issue resource (e.g., `payment-service-oom-kill-1773933600`)

  Namespace of the incident. When omitted, every namespace is searched (first match).

No request body is read. The call adds three annotations to the Issue and returns the updated incident:

| Annotation | Value |
|:-----------|:------|
| `aiops.chatcli.io/acknowledged` | `"true"` |
| `aiops.chatcli.io/acknowledged-at` | Current time (RFC 3339) |
| `aiops.chatcli.io/acknowledged-by` | The **role** of the calling API key (`operator` or `admin`) — not a person's name |

Acknowledging gives the incident an owner. It does not change the incident `state`, but the notification controller reads `aiops.chatcli.io/acknowledged`: an escalation that has not started yet is not started, and a running one stops at its current level, with no further level and no repeat notification. The acknowledgment is recorded on the escalation's entry in the EscalationPolicy `status.activeEscalations` as `acknowledgedAt` and `acknowledgedBy` (the caller's role). State-change notifications, such as `Resolved`, still go out. Acknowledging again simply refreshes the timestamp; there is no conflict error.

