## Subcommands

    The `/storage` command without a REPL, for cron jobs and scripts. Boots no provider.

    | Form | Description |
    | --- | --- |
    | `chatcli storage [store]` | Inventory: files, size, policy and what the rules would remove now, per store |
    | `chatcli storage prune [store]` | Dry run: what the rules would remove, with the reason per item group |
    | `chatcli storage prune [store] --apply` | Remove it |
    | `--json` | Machine-readable inventory or outcome |

    Stores: `costs`, `checkpoints`, `sessions`, `transcripts`, `parked`, `memory-pending`, `attachments`, `taskgraph`, `pulse`, `ccr`, `hub`; every other store (`memory`, `skills`, `plugins`, `contexts`, `agents`, `commands`, `reflexion`, `scheduler`, `tokenizers`, `mcp`, `cache`, `logs`) is inventoried and never pruned. Rules: the session TTL (`CHATCLI_SESSION_TTL`) on last write for machine sessions, transcripts, parks, cost snapshots, pending memory, saved attachments (the private copies of images attached in the web UI) and checkpoints; checkpoints whose workspace is a temp directory or no longer exists; cost snapshots started in a burst (four or more in one minute, at most two requests each — a test suite, never a person) on `prune` only; task-graph runs past 30 days; live-dashboard spools (`pulse`) of every process that is no longer running, never one that is still recording; the CCR archive's TTL and size cap and the hub's idle TTL, swept when applied. Named sessions, distilled memory and user content are never touched. `--apply` without `prune` is refused.
  
    Starts ChatCLI as a gRPC server for remote access (alias `chatcli serve`). Every flag has an environment variable that sets its default.

    | Flag | Env | Description | Default |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `--port <int>` | `CHATCLI_SERVER_PORT` | gRPC port | `50051` |
    | `--token <string>` | `CHATCLI_SERVER_TOKEN` | Shared bearer token (callers get the admin role) | `""` |
    | `--tls-cert <path>` | `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CERT` | TLS certificate (the server accepts TLS 1.3 only). Needs `--tls-key`: one without the other refuses to start instead of serving plaintext | `""` |
    | `--tls-key <path>` | `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_KEY` | TLS private key. Needs `--tls-cert` | `""` |
    | `--tls-client-ca <path>` | `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CLIENT_CA` | CA bundle for client certificates; enables mTLS, every connection must then present a certificate. Requires `--tls-cert` and `--tls-key` | `""` |
    | `--provider <name>` | `LLM_PROVIDER` | Default LLM provider | First configured provider |
    | `--model <name>` | — | Default model | Provider default |
    | `--metrics-port <int>` | `CHATCLI_METRICS_PORT` | Prometheus `/metrics` and `/healthz` over plain HTTP, no authentication, on all interfaces; `0` disables it | `9090` |
    | `--enable-reflection` | `CHATCLI_GRPC_REFLECTION=true` | Registers gRPC server reflection; keep off in production | `false` |
    | `--fallback-providers <list>` | `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` | Comma-separated provider chain, in order; installed only when at least two of the listed providers resolve | `""` |
    | `--fallback-max-retries <n>` | `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_MAX_RETRIES` | Retries per provider before moving on | `2` |
    | `--fallback-cooldown-base <dur>` | `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_COOLDOWN_BASE` | Base cooldown after a provider failure | `30s` |
    | `--fallback-cooldown-max <dur>` | `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_COOLDOWN_MAX` | Maximum cooldown | `5m` |
    | `--mcp-config <path>` | `CHATCLI_MCP_CONFIG` | MCP servers config JSON (`CHATCLI_MCP_ENABLED=true` loads the default path) | `""` |
    | `--watch-config <path>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_CONFIG` | Multi-target watcher config YAML | `""` |
    | `--watch-deployment <name>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_DEPLOYMENT` | Single K8s deployment to monitor (enables the watcher) | `""` |
    | `--watch-namespace <ns>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_NAMESPACE` | Namespace of that deployment | `"default"` |
    | `--watch-interval <dur>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_INTERVAL` | Collection interval | `30s` |
    | `--watch-window <dur>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_WINDOW` | Observation window | `2h` |
    | `--watch-max-log-lines <n>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_MAX_LOG_LINES` | Max log lines per pod | `100` |
    | `--watch-kubeconfig <path>` | `CHATCLI_KUBECONFIG` | Kubeconfig | In-cluster or default |

    There are no flags for the bind address or for JWT: use `CHATCLI_BIND_ADDRESS` (unset means `127.0.0.1`, or `0.0.0.0` inside Kubernetes) and `CHATCLI_JWT_SECRET` / `CHATCLI_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` / `CHATCLI_JWT_ISSUER` / `CHATCLI_JWT_AUDIENCE`. On any bind that is not loopback the server refuses to start without a credential: a token, a client CA (mTLS) or JWT material that loads. JWT material that fails to load also stops the server when it is the only credential. The server answers the standard `grpc.health.v1.Health` service and `/healthz` on the metrics port, both without authentication.
  
    Connects to a remote server via gRPC.

    | Flag | Env | Description | Default |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `<address>` | — | Address (positional) | |
    | `--addr <host:port>` | `CHATCLI_REMOTE_ADDR` | Address (flag) | `""` |
    | `--token <string>` | `CHATCLI_REMOTE_TOKEN` | Sent as `authorization: Bearer`; the shared token or a JWT | `""` |
    | `--provider <name>` | — | Override the server's provider (`DEVIN` is not offered: the server image has no Devin CLI) | `""` |
    | `--model <name>` | — | Override the server's model | `""` |
    | `--llm-key <string>` | `CHATCLI_CLIENT_API_KEY` | Your own LLM API key or OAuth token, forwarded to the server | `""` |
    | `--use-local-auth` | — | Use the credential from `~/.chatcli/auth-profiles.json` | `false` |
    | `--tls` | — | TLS 1.3, verified with `--ca-cert` or the system CAs; the connection is TLS even without it | `false` |
    | `--ca-cert <path>` | — | CA certificate that verifies the server; implies `--tls` | `""` |
    | `--client-id`, `--client-key`, `--realm`, `--agent-id` | — | StackSpot credentials | `""` |
    | `--ollama-url <url>` | — | Ollama base URL | `""` |
    | `-p <prompt>` | — | Remote one-shot | `""` |
    | `--raw` | — | Unformatted output | `false` |
    | `--max-tokens <int>` | — | Max tokens | `0` |

    Without `--tls` the client still dials TLS with the system CAs; a plaintext server needs `CHATCLI_ALLOW_INSECURE=true`. A client certificate for mTLS comes only from `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_CERT` and `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_KEY`, together with `--tls`; there is no flag for it.

    The interactive session is bound to the server like the in-REPL `/connect`: the server's plugins run remotely, `/agent list` and `/agent skills` add the server's entries, `/session` offers remote sessions, `/watch status` queries the server's watcher and `/disconnect` returns to the local provider. See [Remote Connection](/features/remote-connect#remote-plugins-sessions-and-watcher-status).
  
    Monitors K8s workloads with AI.

    | Flag | Env | Description | Default |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `--deployment <name>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_DEPLOYMENT` | Deployment (required unless `--config`) | `""` |
    | `--config <path>` | — | Multi-target watch config YAML | `""` |
    | `--namespace <ns>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_NAMESPACE` | Namespace | `"default"` |
    | `--interval <dur>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_INTERVAL` | Collection interval | `30s` |
    | `--window <dur>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_WINDOW` | Observation window | `2h` |
    | `--max-log-lines <n>` | `CHATCLI_WATCH_MAX_LOG_LINES` | Max log lines per pod | `100` |
    | `--kubeconfig <path>` | `CHATCLI_KUBECONFIG` | Kubeconfig | In-cluster or default |
    | `--provider <name>` | `LLM_PROVIDER` | LLM provider | `.env` |
    | `--model <name>` | — | LLM model | Provider default |
    | `-p <prompt>` | — | One-shot with K8s context | `""` |
    | `--max-tokens <int>` | — | Max tokens | `0` |
  
    One-shot self-update for scripts and automation — the same flow as `/update`, without entering the REPL. Updates through the detected install channel (Homebrew, go install or verified binary self-replace); manual channels (Docker, source build) get instructions instead.

    | Argument | Description |
    | --- | --- |
    | *(none)* | Check and apply through the detected channel |
    | `check` | Report only — never applies |

    Exit codes: `0` updated or already on the latest version (including `check`), `1` check/apply failure or a manual channel with a pending update, `2` invalid usage. See [Auto-Update](/features/auto-update) for channel detection and the verified self-replace pipeline.
  
