TITLE: Environment Variables

# Environment Variables

This page lists **all** environment variables that ChatCLI recognizes. Configure them in your `.env` file or via `export` in the shell.

## General

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `LLM_PROVIDER` | Active provider: `OPENAI`, `OPENAI_ASSISTANT`, `CLAUDEAI`, `BEDROCK`, `GOOGLEAI`, `XAI`, `ZAI`, `MINIMAX`, `MOONSHOT`, `OPENROUTER`, `STACKSPOT`, `OLLAMA`, `COPILOT`, `DEVIN` | Auto-detected |
| `CHATCLI_DOTENV` | Explicit path for the environment file. Without it, ChatCLI looks for `./.env`, then `~/.chatcli/.env`, then `~/.env` — the first that exists wins. The home fallbacks are what keep `chatcli acp` and `chatcli mcp-server` configured when an editor or MCP client spawns them without your shell environment. `/config` shows the file in effect and its origin. | `.env` → `~/.chatcli/.env` → `~/.env` |
| `CHATCLI_PROJECT_ENV` | Policy for the `.env` of the project an ACP client announces on `session/new`: `safe` (default) applies it fill-only and refuses credential/endpoint variables (`*_API_KEY`, `*_TOKEN`, `*_BASE_URL`, `*_API_URL`, …) because a project directory is untrusted input; `all` applies every key; `off` ignores project files. It never overrides a variable already in effect, and only the first project announced applies. | `safe` |
| `CHATCLI_MANAGED_CONFIG` | Path of the organization-managed file (defaults with `KEY=value`, locked policies with `!KEY=value`), applied at boot and re-applied on `/reload`. Defaults to `/etc/chatcli/managed.env` (Linux/macOS) or `%ProgramData%\chatcli\managed.env` (Windows). See [Security → Managed Configuration](/features/security#managed-configuration-organization-defaults-and-locked-policies). | _(platform path)_ |
| `CHATCLI_LANG` | Force interface language (`pt-BR`, `en`) | Auto-detected |
| `CHATCLI_IGNORE` | Path to `.chatignore` rules file | Auto-detected |
| `CHATCLI_THEME` | Interface color theme (chat, cards, markdown, spinners). 12 themes: `dark`, `light`, `grafite` + 9 community palettes (dracula, nord, tokyo-night, solarized-dark/light, gruvbox, catppuccin-mocha, monokai, one-dark). Switch at runtime via `/config ui theme`. See the [Theme System](/features/ui-theme). | `dark` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Log level: `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error` | `info` |
| `LOG_FILE` | Log file path (`CHATCLI_LOG_FILE` is an alias; `LOG_FILE` wins when both are set) | `~/.chatcli/app.log` |
| `LOG_MAX_SIZE` | Maximum log size before rotation (`CHATCLI_LOG_MAX_SIZE_MB`, in MB, overrides it) | `100MB` |
| `CHATCLI_LOG_STDERR` | `chatcli server` and `chatcli gateway` only: `true`/`false` forces the JSON log lines on stderr on or off. Unset, they are on whenever stderr is not a terminal (containers, systemd, pipes), so `kubectl logs` and `docker logs` carry the log; an interactive terminal keeps the file only. Not duplicated under `CHATCLI_ENV=dev`. | auto |
| `CHATCLI_ENV` | Logging mode: `dev` (colored console on stdout + file), `prod` (JSON file; services add stderr, see `CHATCLI_LOG_STDERR`). Backward-compatible with legacy `ENV`. | `prod` |
| `MAX_RETRIES` | Maximum retries for API calls | `5` |
| `INITIAL_BACKOFF` | Initial time between retries (seconds) | `3` |
| `HISTORY_FILE` | Path to history file (supports `~`) | `.chatcli_history` |
| `HISTORY_MAX_SIZE` | Maximum history size before rotation | `100MB` |

---

## LLM Providers

### OpenAI

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | API key | -- |
| `OPENAI_MODEL` | Model to use | `gpt-5.4` |
| `OPENAI_ASSISTANT_MODEL` | Model for assistant (agent mode). OpenAI shut down the Assistants API endpoint on Aug 26, 2026 — prefer the `OPENAI` provider | `gpt-4o` |
| `OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS` | Response token limit | `60000` |
| `OPENAI_USE_RESPONSES` | Force the Responses API for every model. Note: `false` does not force Chat Completions — OAuth sessions and models whose catalog entry prefers Responses (e.g. `gpt-5.4`, the default) still use it | `false` |
| `OPENAI_API_URL` | Custom Chat Completions endpoint. Must be the **full** URL (ending in `/chat/completions`); the `/models` listing URL is derived from it. With a custom host, the model listing is not filtered by family — every model the gateway returns is listed. Requests keep sending `OPENAI_API_KEY` as the Bearer token, so set it to the gateway's key | `https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions` |
| `OPENAI_RESPONSES_API_URL` | Custom Responses API endpoint. Set it together with `OPENAI_API_URL` when redirecting the provider to a compatible endpoint | `https://api.openai.com/v1/responses` |

### Anthropic (Claude)

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | API key | -- |
| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | Model to use (e.g., `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) | `claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| `ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS` | Response token limit | `20000` |
| `ANTHROPIC_API_VERSION` | API version | `2023-06-01` |
| `ANTHROPIC_SPEED` | Set to `fast` to opt in to **fast mode on Opus 5.5 / Opus 4.8** (research preview, ~2.5× output tokens/sec at premium pricing — $8/$40 on Opus 5.5). Silently ignored on models without the `fast_mode` catalog capability — safe to leave set when switching models. | -- |
| `ANTHROPIC_1MTOKENS_SONNET` | Enable the 1M-context beta header on Sonnet 4.x OAuth requests. Opus 4.7/4.8 already ship with 1M native context and ignore this flag. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION` | Claude Code release the OAuth surface presents (`claude-cli/X.Y.Z`), when newer than the compiled floor. Normally unnecessary: the API gates new models by release (`claude_code_version_too_old`) and ChatCLI learns the required release from that error and resends the request. `/config` shows the effective value. | -- |

### AWS Bedrock (full catalog)

`BEDROCK` provider — invokes the **entire Bedrock catalog** (Anthropic, OpenAI, Llama, Nova, Mistral, Cohere, AI21, DeepSeek, Moonshot Kimi (also available directly via `MOONSHOT`), MiniMax, Qwen, Z.AI/GLM, Gemma, Nemotron, TwelveLabs, and any provider AWS adds) using the SDK's credential chain (env vars, `~/.aws/credentials`, SSO via `~/.aws/config`, IAM role). Activation requires real credentials — the mere existence of `~/.aws/config` with only region/output does not activate Bedrock.

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `BEDROCK_MODEL` | Default model when none is selected; catalog aliases work (`claude-opus-4-8`) | `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| `BEDROCK_PROVIDER` | Schema override: `anthropic` / `claude`, `openai` / `gpt`, `converse` / `auto`. Overrides prefix auto-detection for Claude, OpenAI and opaque ids; Converse-only vendors (`amazon.`/Nova, `meta.`, `mistral.`, `cohere.`, `ai21.`, `deepseek.`, …) always keep the Converse API — a conflicting override is ignored with a warning. | auto-detect |
| `BEDROCK_TEMPERATURE` | Temperature (used by OpenAI and Converse paths) | -- |
| `BEDROCK_TOP_P` | Top-p sampling (used by the Converse path) | -- |
| `BEDROCK_REGION` | AWS region (takes precedence over `AWS_REGION`) | -- |
| `AWS_REGION` | AWS region (fallback) | -- |
| `BEDROCK_PROFILE` | Profile scoped to ChatCLI — takes precedence over `AWS_PROFILE` and leaves the rest of your shell untouched. Honored by chat, agent, model listing, embeddings and image generation. | -- |
| `AWS_PROFILE` | Profile in `~/.aws/credentials` or `~/.aws/config` (SSO, `aws login`/`login_session`, assume-role, credential_process). Can be set in the environment file — but note that an editor-spawned `acp`/`mcp-server` only sees it if the file is discovered (see `CHATCLI_DOTENV`) or the client passes it in its `env` block. `/config` shows the effective profile and the variable it came from. | -- |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` | Static credentials | -- |
| `AWS_CA_BUNDLE` | PEM bundle read natively by the SDK | -- |
| `BEDROCK_BASE_URL` | Custom base URL for the whole Bedrock surface (VPC endpoints, corporate DNS) — parity with Claude Code's `ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_BASE_URL`; wins over `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL*`. Applies to chat, embeddings, image generation and model listing. | -- |
| `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK_RUNTIME` | Override for Bedrock Runtime endpoint (VPC endpoints) | -- |
| `BEDROCK_CONTROL_BASE_URL` | Optional control-plane override (model listing in `/switch`) for split hosts — VPC endpoints are per service; wins over `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK` | inherits `BEDROCK_BASE_URL` |
| `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_BEDROCK` | Override for Bedrock (control plane) endpoint | -- |
| `AWS_EC2_METADATA_DISABLED` | `true` explicitly disables IMDS (169.254.169.254) | -- |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_ENABLE_IMDS` | `1`/`true` forces IMDS probe on non-EC2 machines | `false` |
| `BEDROCK_MAX_TOKENS` | Response token limit | From catalog |
| `BEDROCK_ANTHROPIC_ENDPOINT` | Claude wire routing: `auto` (default) is catalog-driven — Opus 5.5, Opus 5, Sonnet 5, Fable 5 and Fable 5.1 go to the Messages endpoint automatically and fall back to legacy `InvokeModel` if the Mantle call fails; `mantle` pins the Messages endpoint (no fallback); `invoke` pins legacy `InvokeModel`. | `auto` |
| `BEDROCK_MANTLE_BASE_URL` | Messages endpoint override (`bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws`) for VPC endpoints/proxies | -- |
| `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` | Short-lived bearer token (`aws-bedrock-token-generator`) — sent in the Messages endpoint's `x-api-key` header, no SigV4 | -- |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_CA_BUNDLE` | Bedrock-specific PEM bundle. Overrides `AWS_CA_BUNDLE` and the global `CHATCLI_CA_BUNDLE` (which acts as fallback). See [Global TLS Trust](#global-tls-trust-corporate-proxy). | -- |
| `CHATCLI_BEDROCK_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY` | `true` disables TLS verification (insecure, troubleshooting only). Overrides the global `CHATCLI_TLS_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY` (which acts as fallback). | `false` |

Modern models on Bedrock (Claude 3.7+/4.x/4.5/4.6/4.7 and equivalents from other providers) require **inference profile IDs** (prefix `global.`, `us.`, `eu.`, or `apac.`). `/switch --model` automatically filters out base IDs that don't support `ON_DEMAND`, so only invokable IDs + profiles appear in the listing. See [AWS Bedrock](/features/bedrock) for details.

