## Agent Mode

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_CMD_TIMEOUT` | Timeout per executed command (Go duration: `30s`, `2m`, `10m`) | `10m` |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_DENYLIST` | Extra regex patterns to block commands (separated by `;`) | -- |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_ALLOW_SUDO` | Allow `sudo` without automatic blocking | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_INLINE_CODE_STRICT` | For `python -c` / `node -e` / `perl -e` / `ruby -e` / `php -r` / `lua -e` invocations, treat inline source as **dangerous unless proven safe** (conservative mode). Default: the classifier accepts read-only one-liners (`print(1)`, `import sys; print(sys.version)`) and only blocks patterns with `os.system`, `subprocess`, `socket`, `eval`, `exec`, file writes, network. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_PLUGIN_MAX_TURNS` | Maximum agent turns | `50` |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_PLUGIN_TIMEOUT` | Total agent plugin timeout | `15m` |
| `CHATCLI_AGENT_SKILL_RESCAN` | Re-scan skill `triggers:`/`paths:` on **every ReAct turn** against the model's own reasoning, the file paths in its tool calls, and mid-session follow-ups. Newly matched skills are injected mid-task, **drip-limited to 3 new skills per injection** (the rest re-candidate on the next boundary); a skill collapsed by aging can re-trigger after its cooldown. Accepts `0`/`false`/`off`/`no` to disable. | `1` (on) |
| `CHATCLI_SKILL_INJECT_BUDGET` | Character budget for injected skill **bodies** per system-prompt block; the cumulative **per-run** budget is 2× this value, after which new activations degrade to source pointers. Skills past a budget keep header + description + `Source:` path — nothing lost, only deferred. `0` = unlimited (legacy inline-everything, disables the run cap too). Surfaced in `/config agent`. See [Skill Registry](/features/skill-registry#skill-injection-budget). | `24000` |
| `CHATCLI_COMMANDS` | Master switch for [slash-command templates](/features/slash-commands) (`.chatcli/commands` + `~/.chatcli/commands`, plus interop with Claude Code, Devin, Windsurf, Cursor, opencode, Codex, Gemini CLI, Qwen Code and GitHub Copilot command dirs). Catalog shown in `/config commands`. | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_COMMANDS_AUTOROUTE` | Auto-route commands whose resolved mode is coder (explicit `mode: coder` or inferred from `allowed-tools`) from chat into a coder one-shot run — see [slash commands](/features/slash-commands). | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_CHAT_CODER_HANDOFF` | In chat mode the assistant may propose switching to coder mode for a task that needs the workspace; you confirm at the prompt (Enter or `y`) before anything runs — see [coder mode](/core-concepts/coder-mode#handoff-from-chat). `false` turns the proposal off. | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_SKILL_AGE_TURNS` | Agent/coder skill lifecycle: a mid-loop skill block older than this many turns collapses to a one-line stub (full guidance archived, recoverable via `@recall`; the skill leaves the dedup set and can re-trigger after the same number of turns). | `6` |
| `CHATCLI_HISTORY_REWRITE_PRESSURE` | Share (0 to 1) of the compaction budget the history must reach before microcompact, repeated-read dedup and skill aging rewrite messages ahead of a warm provider prefix cache; every provider with a prompt cache bills such a rewrite as a cache write of the whole tail. `0` restores the age-only behavior (rewrite every turn). Applies to the orchestrator loop and to workers. | `0.75` |

