| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Required for `provider=openai` (shared with chat) | — |
| `BEDROCK_REGION` / `AWS_REGION` / `AWS_PROFILE` / AWS credentials | Required for `provider=bedrock` — reuses the same chain as chat. | per chat Bedrock |

**Bedrock embeddings** support `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` (default), `amazon.titan-embed-text-v1`, `cohere.embed-english-v3`, `cohere.embed-multilingual-v3`, `cohere.embed-v4:0` (plus `us.`/`eu.`/`global.` profile ids) and `amazon.nova-2-multimodal-embeddings-v1:0` (Nova MME). Titan and Nova MME parallelize batches with an 8-worker pool (their APIs accept only 1 text per call); Cohere sends the entire batch in one call. Dispatch is automatic from the model id prefix. See [RAG + HyDE](/features/quality/rag-hyde) and [AWS Bedrock](/features/bedrock).

