## Provider Fallback

Read by `chatcli server` (each variable is the default of the matching `--fallback-*` flag). `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` is also the extraction fallback list for long-term memory when `CHATCLI_MEMORY_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` is unset.

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` | Comma-separated providers, tried in the order listed. The server builds the chain from this list alone: the primary provider (`--provider` / `LLM_PROVIDER`) is **not** added for you, so list it first. The chain is installed only when at least two listed providers resolve, and it serves only requests that carry no caller credentials and name no provider or model. The server Helm chart (`fallback.*`) and the operator (`spec.fallback`) put the primary provider first for you. | -- |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_MODEL_` | Model for that provider in the chain (for example `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_MODEL_CLAUDEAI`). When unset, the primary provider keeps the server model (`--model`), and any other provider runs its own default model: its model variable (for example `OPENAI_MODEL`), then the built-in default. | primary: server model; others: the provider's default |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_MAX_RETRIES` | Retries per provider before advancing | `2` |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_COOLDOWN_BASE` | Base cooldown after failure (Go duration) | `30s` |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_COOLDOWN_MAX` | Maximum cooldown (exponential backoff) | `5m` |
| `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_ENABLED` | Not read by the server, and not set by the Helm chart or the operator; `/config` labels it as not read when it is set. A non-empty `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` is the only switch, and the chain is installed when it resolves two or more providers. | -- |

