| `CHATCLI_LATEST_VERSION_URL` | Custom URL for version check | GitHub API |

### Context and memory threat scan

Sanitizes **injected** prompt content — contexts attached via `/context attach` and long-term memory — against prompt-injection before sending it to the model.

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_THREATSCAN` | Toggle the context/memory threat scan. On by default; accepts `false`/`0`/`off`/`no` to disable. | `true` (on) |

### Server Security

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_JWT_SECRET` | HS256 shared secret the server verifies bearer JWTs with (tokens must carry `exp`). A value that resolves to PEM key material selects RS256 instead. If it looks like key material but cannot be loaded and JWT is the only credential, the server refuses to start; with a shared token or client certificates also configured it keeps serving and only JWT callers are refused. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` | RSA public key (inline PEM, or a path to one) that selects RS256 and wins over `CHATCLI_JWT_SECRET`. A key that cannot be loaded follows the same fail-closed rule. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_JWT_ISSUER` | Expected JWT issuer claim | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_JWT_AUDIENCE` | Expected JWT audience claim | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_RATE_LIMIT_RPS` | Rate limit: sustained requests per second, per authenticated subject (JWT `sub`, `mtls:<name>`; every shared-token caller shares the one `legacy-token` bucket), else per peer address. Always on — values ≤ 0 keep the default. Exceeding it returns `ResourceExhausted` with `retry after N seconds` and a `retry-after` header (the refill time of one token, rounded up, at least 1), on unary calls and streams alike. | `10` |
| `CHATCLI_RATE_LIMIT_BURST` | Rate limit: burst capacity | `20` |
| `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CLIENT_CA` | CA bundle client certificates are verified against (flag `--tls-client-ca`). Enables mutual TLS: every connection must then present a valid client certificate, and TLS (`--tls-cert`/`--tls-key`) is required. Counts as a credential for the bind guard. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_MTLS_ROLE` | Role granted to a caller identified by its verified client certificate alone (no bearer token): `viewer`/`readonly`, `operator`/`user` or `admin`. An unrecognized value resolves to read-only; a bearer token still wins | `user` |
| `CHATCLI_MAX_RECV_MSG_SIZE` | Maximum gRPC receive message size (bytes) | `52428800` (50MB) |
| `CHATCLI_MAX_SEND_MSG_SIZE` | Maximum gRPC send message size (bytes) | `52428800` (50MB) |
| `CHATCLI_MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS` | Maximum concurrent gRPC streams per connection | `100` |
| `CHATCLI_BIND_ADDRESS` | Interface the gRPC listener binds to. Unset: `127.0.0.1`, or `0.0.0.0` when `KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST` is set (inside a pod). On any non-loopback bind the server refuses to start without a credential — `CHATCLI_SERVER_TOKEN`, `CHATCLI_JWT_SECRET`, `CHATCLI_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` or `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CLIENT_CA`. | `127.0.0.1` / `0.0.0.0` (K8s) |
| `CHATCLI_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` | Path for the structured audit log file. Must be **absolute** — relative values are rejected with a logged error. Lines are hash-chained (`seq`, `prev_hash`, `hash`); `/config security verify-audit` checks the chain. | `""` |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | OpenTelemetry standard: base URL of an OTLP/HTTP collector; ChatCLI pushes its token, cache, compaction, embedding and cost counters as cumulative sums to `<base>/v1/metrics` (JSON encoding, no SDK). Off when unset. See [Server mode → OpenTelemetry export](/features/server-mode#opentelemetry-export-otlp). | `""` |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT` | OpenTelemetry standard: full metrics URL, wins over the base endpoint. | derived |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS` | OpenTelemetry standard: `k=v,k2=v2` request headers (values URL-encoded), e.g. an `Authorization` token. | `""` |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | OpenTelemetry standard: `service.name` resource attribute. | `chatcli` |
| `OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL` | OpenTelemetry standard: push interval in milliseconds (minimum 1000). | `60000` |
| `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` | OpenTelemetry standard: extra `k=v,k2=v2` resource attributes; ChatCLI adds `chatcli.surface` and `chatcli.tenant`. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_LOG_FILE` / `CHATCLI_LOG_MAX_SIZE_MB` / `CHATCLI_LOG_MAX_BACKUPS` / `CHATCLI_LOG_MAX_AGE_DAYS` / `CHATCLI_LOG_COMPRESS` | Rotation of the log file, for every command: `CHATCLI_LOG_FILE` is an alias of `LOG_FILE`; `CHATCLI_LOG_MAX_SIZE_MB` (in MB) overrides `LOG_MAX_SIZE`; then the number of rotated files kept, their age in days, and gzip compression (`false` to keep them plain). The Instance field `spec.features.logRotation` sets them; the server Helm chart sets them from `logging` (20 MB, 3 backups, 28 days, `true`), and an `extraEnv` entry of the same name wins. | defaults: `LOG_FILE`, 100 MB, 3 backups, 28 days, `true` |
| `CHATCLI_DEBUG` | `true` makes the server's recovery interceptors log the full panic value and stack trace; otherwise only a request ID and a sanitized, truncated message are logged | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_ALLOW_HTTP_PROVIDERS` | Server: allow `http://` (non-TLS) provider base URLs that callers send through provider config (the SSRF validator refuses them otherwise) | `false` |

