### Coder Execution (auto-diagnostics, checkpoints, sandbox)

Governance for what `@coder` runs and how it recovers — all apply to `/coder` and `/agent`.

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_CODER_AUTODIAG` | After a successful `@coder` `write`/`patch`/`multipatch`, auto-inject the touched files' **LSP diagnostics** into the tool result as a `[DIAGNOSTICS]` block, so the model sees a broken file immediately instead of turns later. Silent on clean files; capped at 5 files / 3000 chars. Accepts `off`/`0`/`false`/`no` to disable. | `on` |
| `CHATCLI_CODER_CHECKPOINTS` | Automatic **shadow-git** workspace snapshots taken before every mutating `@coder` subcommand (`write`/`patch`/`multipatch`/`exec`), so you can rewind with `@coder checkpoint --restore <hash>`. Snapshots live under `~/.chatcli/checkpoints` and never touch your project's `.git`. Accepts `off` to disable. | `on` |
| `CHATCLI_CODER_CHECKPOINT_TIMEOUT` | Hard deadline for one checkpoint snapshot, in whole seconds (clamped to 10 minutes). Snapshots are also bounded by a root guard (your home directory, or any directory containing it, is never auto-snapshotted) and a circuit breaker (three consecutive failures disable automatic snapshots for the session). | `10` (auto) / `60` (manual) |
| `CHATCLI_CODER_SANDBOX` | **OS-level confinement** for `@coder exec`: `off` (default) · `workspace` (writes confined to the workspace + build caches) · `strict` (workspace + **no network**) · `docker`/`podman`/`container` (force the portable container backend). Native `sandbox-exec` (macOS) / `bwrap` (Linux) / Docker · Podman container (**any OS, Windows included**); degrades to unconfined with a note when no backend exists. | `off` |
| `CHATCLI_CODER_SANDBOX_IMAGE` | Container image for the Docker/Podman sandbox backend. Host toolchains (go, node…) live in the image. | `alpine:3` |

### Plugin and Auth Security

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_ALLOW_UNSIGNED_PLUGINS` | Allow unsigned plugins to execute | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_PLUGIN_QUARANTINE` | Hold newly seen unsigned plugins before they can run: a duration, `on` (24h), or `off` | `off` |
| `CHATCLI_ALLOW_INSECURE` | `chatcli connect` and the in-REPL `/connect` only: without `--tls`, `true` dials the server in plaintext; otherwise the client still dials TLS 1.3 with the system CAs. It has no effect on the server listener. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_CERT` | `chatcli connect`: client certificate presented for mTLS; read only together with `--tls` (there is no flag) | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_KEY` | `chatcli connect`: key of that client certificate; required when `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_CERT` is set | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_ENCRYPTION_KEY` | Opt-in encryption at rest for saved sessions, autosaves, MCP session mirrors, park snapshots, the transcript journal, long-term memory JSON stores, knowledge contexts, the CCR archive and cost snapshots (AES-256-GCM, key derived with HKDF; plaintext files migrate on next save). See [Security](/features/security#encryption-at-rest-sessions-memory-contexts-archives-costs). | `""` (off) |
| `CHATCLI_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS` | Comma-separated retired secrets that still open stores sealed before a key rotation; writes use the current key only. Run `/config security reseal` to migrate every store, then unset it. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_KEYCHAIN_BACKEND` | Keychain backend: `auto`, `file`, `keychain`. On `auto` a test binary never touches the OS keychain; `keychain` forces it | `auto` |
| `CHATCLI_DISABLE_HISTORY` | Disable conversation history recording | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_TTL` | Machine-session time-to-live, in days (`0` disables; user-named sessions never expire) | `90d` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_AUTOSAVE` | Auto-save the conversation on interactive REPL exit | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_AUTOSAVE_KEEP` | Keep-count backstop per machine-session prefix (newest survive) | `600` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_WRITETHROUGH` | Cross-surface continuity for the active named session: write each turn through to the session file and adopt writes made by other surfaces (REPL, MCP/ACP server, gateway) before each turn. `false` disables both directions. See [Cross-surface continuity](/features/session-management#cross-surface-continuity). | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_AUTORECALL` | Proactive saved-session recall: each chat, agent and coder turn searches the saved sessions for the current topic and injects a short `[SESSION RECALL]` pointer block (agent/coder: read with `@session get`; chat: attach with `/session attach`). Shown in `/config session`. `false` disables it. | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_SESSION_TRANSCRIPT` | Append-only transcript journal under `~/.chatcli/transcripts/<id>.jsonl`: every message is appended once (fsynced) at turn boundaries and after each agent tool batch, and history rewrites (compaction, `/compact`, microcompact) are recorded as events instead of being lost — the durable full record behind the compacted in-memory window. Sealed line by line when `CHATCLI_ENCRYPTION_KEY` is set; expires with the machine-session TTL. `false` disables it. See [Transcript journal](/features/session-management#transcript-journal). | `true` |
| `CHATCLI_ENV_REDACT_MODE` | Secret redaction on everything the model receives from tools, files and the memory extractor: `permissive` (name denylist + value shapes), `strict` (also redacts `KEY=VALUE` lines not on the safe allowlist), `off`. See [Security](/features/security#secret-redaction-on-the-llm-path). | `permissive` |
| `CHATCLI_REDACT_PATTERNS` | Extra variable-name fragments treated as sensitive (comma-separated, case-insensitive substring) | `""` |

### Operator Security

These variables are read by the **operator** process (the `chatcli-operator` Deployment), not by the server pods it manages. Set them through the `chatcli-operator` Helm values named in each row, or `extraEnv`.

The REST API and web dashboard authenticate with the `X-API-Key` header. Keys are a YAML list of `{key, role, description}` (roles `viewer`, `operator`, `admin`) under the key `api-keys` of the Secret `chatcli-operator-secrets`, else of the ConfigMap `chatcli-operator-config`, in the operator namespace; they are re-read every 30s. The chart renders the Secret when `apiKeys.create=true` with `apiKeys.entries`. With no key configured, every `/api/` call is refused unless `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_DEV_MODE=true`. Requests without a valid key are rate limited at 30 per minute per client host, and each valid key at 600 per minute.

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_DEV_MODE` | `true` admits every REST/dashboard call as `admin` while **no** API key is configured (once a key exists, keys are enforced). Read with boolean semantics, case-insensitively: `true`, `TRUE`, `1` and `t` turn it on, anything else (unset included) leaves it off; the auth check, the rate limiter and the startup log share this one parse. Development only. Helm: `security.devMode`. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_ALERT_TRANSPORT` | How the WatcherBridge receives alerts: `stream` (StreamAlerts, polling only while the server lacks it) or `poll` (every 30s). Any other value stops the operator at startup. Helm: `alertTransport`. | `stream` |
| `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_DECISION_ENGINE` | `true` gates every RemediationPlan on adjusted AI confidence, severity and a per-namespace circuit breaker. Helm: `decisionEngine.enabled`. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_CLUSTER_NAME` | This cluster's ClusterRegistration name; its tier decides which severities wait for a human. A name no ClusterRegistration carries sends every plan to manual approval. Helm: `clusterName`. | empty (off) |
| `CHATCLI_AIOPS_PORT` | Port of the REST API and web dashboard (served on every operator replica). Helm: `api.port`. | `8090` |
| `CHATCLI_AIOPS_TLS_CERT` / `CHATCLI_AIOPS_TLS_KEY` | Paths, inside the operator container, of the certificate and key for the REST API and dashboard. With both set they serve HTTPS (TLS 1.3 minimum); otherwise plain HTTP. Mount the Secret with the chart's `extraVolumes`/`extraVolumeMounts`. Helm: `security.apiTLS.certFile` / `keyFile`. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_GRPC_TLS_CERT` / `CHATCLI_GRPC_TLS_KEY` | Operator-wide client certificate and key the operator presents to Instances (mTLS) when an Instance sets no `spec.server.security.operatorClientCertSecretName`. Both are required together. Helm: `security.grpcTLS.certFile` / `keyFile`. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_GRPC_TLS_CA` | Operator-wide CA bundle used to verify the **server** certificate of an Instance whose `spec.server.tls.secretName` Secret has no `ca.crt` (a `ca.crt` in that Secret wins; with neither, the system CAs are used). Must be an **absolute** path. The operator always dials Instances over TLS 1.3 — see the [production setup cookbook](/cookbook/aiops-production-setup). Helm: `security.grpcTLS.caFile`. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_ALLOWED_RESOURCE_TYPES` | Extra resource kinds (comma-separated) the `ApplyManifest` remediation may create or update, added to the built-in list; other kinds are refused. Helm: `security.allowedResourceTypes`. | 16 built-in kinds (workloads, Service, ConfigMap, HPA, PDB, Ingress, Prometheus Operator and Istio kinds) |
| `CHATCLI_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | Origins allowed to call the operator REST API from a browser (comma-separated, or `*`). Helm: `security.corsAllowedOrigins` (list). | `""` (deny all) |
| `CHATCLI_CORS_ORIGIN` | A single allowed origin, appended to `CHATCLI_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. Helm: `security.corsOrigin`. | `""` |
| `CHATCLI_CORS_ALLOWED_METHODS` | Methods allowed cross-origin (comma-separated). Helm: `security.corsAllowedMethods` (list). | `GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS` |
| `CHATCLI_CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS` | Allow cookies and `Authorization` on cross-origin requests. Helm: `security.corsAllowCredentials`. | `false` |
| `CHATCLI_ALLOWED_DIAGNOSTIC_COMMANDS` | Additional commands accepted by `ExecDiagnostic` (comma-separated, exact strings, appended to the 100-entry built-in allowlist — see [k8s-operator#execdiagnostic-allowlist](/features/k8s-operator#execdiagnostic-allowlist)). Set it on the operator, not on an Instance. Helm: `security.allowedDiagnosticCommands`. | `""` (defaults only) |
| `CHATCLI_OPERATOR_APP_VERSION` | Default server image tag for Instances that omit `spec.image.tag`. The Helm chart sets it to its `appVersion` and the raw `operator/config/manager/manager.yaml` pins it to the release, so upgrading the operator also rolls those Instances. Unset, Instances fall back to `latest`. Do not set it by hand. | set by chart / manifest |
| `CHATCLI_LOG_SCRUB_PATTERNS` | Extra regular expressions (comma-separated; invalid ones are skipped) scrubbed from the pod logs the operator sends to the LLM for AIInsight analysis, on top of the built-in secret patterns. Helm: `security.logScrubPatterns`. | built-in patterns |
| `POD_NAMESPACE` | Namespace where the operator reads its API-key Secret/ConfigMap. Unset, the service-account namespace is used, then `chatcli-system`. | auto |

