| `CHATCLI_SERVER_PORT` | gRPC server port (flag `--port`) | `50051` |
| `CHATCLI_SERVER_TOKEN` | Shared bearer token (flag `--token`); callers authenticated with it get the `admin` role. On a non-loopback bind a token, JWT material or a client CA is mandatory — see `CHATCLI_BIND_ADDRESS`. | -- |
| `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CERT` | TLS certificate path (flag `--tls-cert`); the server serves TLS 1.3 only. Needs `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_KEY`: one without the other stops the server at startup (`refusing to start a plaintext listener`) | -- |
| `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_KEY` | TLS key path (flag `--tls-key`). Needs `CHATCLI_SERVER_TLS_CERT` | -- |

`chatcli server` also answers the standard `grpc.health.v1.Health` service (no authentication) besides its own `Health` RPC, so kubelet gRPC probes (plaintext servers only — they cannot do TLS), `grpc-health-probe` and load balancers can check it. The security, JWT, metrics and bind variables are under [Server Security](#server-security) and [Metrics and Observability](#metrics-and-observability).

---

## Remote Client

| Variable | Description | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CHATCLI_REMOTE_ADDR` | Server address `host:port` (flag `--addr`, or the first positional argument) | -- |
| `CHATCLI_REMOTE_TOKEN` | Bearer token (flag `--token`): the server's shared token or a JWT | -- |
| `CHATCLI_CLIENT_API_KEY` | Your own LLM API key or OAuth token, forwarded to the server (flag `--llm-key`) | -- |

TLS is chosen with `--tls` and `--ca-cert` (a CA file implies `--tls`); the mTLS client certificate comes only from `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_CERT` / `CHATCLI_TLS_CLIENT_KEY`, and a plaintext server needs `CHATCLI_ALLOW_INSECURE=true` (see [Plugin and Auth Security](#plugin-and-auth-security)).

